   692→    title: Task Queries
   693→    type: feature
   694→    status:
   695→      maturity: draft
   696→      implementation: implemented
   697→    priority: high
   698→    tags:
   699→      - mvp
   700→      - tasks
   701→    description: |
   702→      The key task query: "what can I work on?"
   703→      `kspec tasks ready` is the primary interface for agents and humans.
   704→    acceptance_criteria:
   705→      - id: ac-query-1
   706→        given: tasks with various states and dependencies
   707→        when: kspec tasks ready runs
   708→        then: only tasks that are pending with met dependencies shown
   709→      - id: ac-query-2
   710→        given: ready tasks exist
   711→        when: kspec tasks next runs
   712→        then: highest priority ready task returned
   713→      - id: ac-query-3
   714→        given: multiple ready tasks exist with the same priority
   715→        when: kspec tasks ready runs
   716→        then: tasks are ordered by creation time ascending (oldest first within priority tier)
   717→    requirements:
   718→      - _ulid: 01JHNKA7W1TQRY100000000000
   719→        slugs:
   720→          - query-ready
   721→        title: Ready Tasks Query
   722→        type: requirement
   723→        status:
   724→          maturity: draft
   725→          implementation: implemented
   726→        description: |
   727→          kspec tasks ready
   728→
   729→          Returns tasks where:
   730→          - status = pending
   731→          - all depends_on tasks are completed
   732→          - no manual blocked_by entries
   733→
   734→          This is THE command for "what can I work on next?"
   735→        implements:
   736→          - "@task-queries"
   737→      - _ulid: 01JHNKA7W2TQRY200000000000
   738→        slugs:
