   776→    slugs:
   777→      - tasks-assess-automation
   778→    title: Task Automation Assessment
   779→    type: feature
   780→    tags: []
   781→    description: CLI command to assess task automation eligibility based on criteria (has spec_ref, spec
   782→      has ACs, not spike). Provides visibility into task readiness for automation and enables fast
   783→      triage of obvious cases via --auto mode.
   784→    depends_on: []
   785→    implements: []
   786→    relates_to: []
   787→    tests: []
   788→    traits: []
   789→    notes: []
   790→    created: 2026-01-20T20:52:20.356Z
   791→    acceptance_criteria:
   792→      - id: ac-1
   793→        given: kspec tasks assess automation is run
   794→        when: displaying results
   795→        then: lists pending tasks without automation field (unassessed) by default
   796→      - id: ac-2
   797→        given: kspec tasks assess automation is run
   798→        when: the --all flag is provided
   799→        then: includes tasks that already have automation set
   800→      - id: ac-3
   801→        given: kspec tasks assess automation is run
   802→        when: displaying each task
   803→        then: "shows criteria check results: has_spec_ref, spec_has_acs, not_spike with pass/fail status"
   804→      - id: ac-4
   805→        given: kspec tasks assess automation is run
   806→        when: displaying each task
   807→        then: shows recommendation (review_for_eligible, needs_review, or manual_only)
   808→      - id: ac-5
   809→        given: kspec tasks assess automation is run
   810→        when: output completes
   811→        then: shows summary counts of recommendations at end
   812→      - id: ac-6
   813→        given: kspec tasks assess automation @task-ref is run
   814→        when: a specific task reference is provided
   815→        then: assesses only that task
   816→      - id: ac-7
   817→        given: kspec tasks assess automation @task-ref is run
   818→        when: task is not found
   819→        then: returns non-zero exit code
   820→      - id: ac-8
   821→        given: assessing a task
   822→        when: task has spec_ref pointing to resolvable spec
   823→        then: has_spec_ref criterion passes
   824→      - id: ac-9
   825→        given: assessing a task
   826→        when: spec_ref is missing or unresolvable
   827→        then: has_spec_ref criterion fails
   828→      - id: ac-10
   829→        given: assessing a task with spec_ref
   830→        when: linked spec has at least one acceptance criterion
   831→        then: spec_has_acs criterion passes
   832→      - id: ac-11
   833→        given: assessing a task
   834→        when: task has no spec_ref
   835→        then: spec_has_acs criterion is skipped (neutral)
   836→      - id: ac-12
   837→        given: assessing a task
   838→        when: task type is not spike
   839→        then: not_spike criterion passes
   840→      - id: ac-13
   841→        given: assessing a task
   842→        when: task type is spike
   843→        then: not_spike criterion fails
   844→      - id: ac-14
   845→        given: computing recommendation
   846→        when: task is a spike
   847→        then: recommends manual_only regardless of other criteria
   848→      - id: ac-15
   849→        given: computing recommendation
   850→        when: spec_ref is missing or spec has no ACs
   851→        then: recommends needs_review
   852→      - id: ac-16
   853→        given: computing recommendation
   854→        when: all criteria pass (has spec, has ACs, not spike)
   855→        then: recommends review_for_eligible (agent/human must verify spec/AC adequacy)
   856→      - id: ac-17
   857→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --auto is run
   858→        when: processing tasks
   859→        then: "applies only obvious cases: spikes -> manual_only, missing criteria -> needs_review"
   860→      - id: ac-18
   861→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --auto is run
   862→        when: task passes all criteria
   863→        then: does NOT mark task as eligible (requires agent/human review)
   864→      - id: ac-19
   865→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --auto is run
   866→        when: marking a task
   867→        then: adds note to task explaining the assessment
   868→      - id: ac-20
   869→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --auto is run
   870→        when: marking task as needs_review
   871→        then: note includes reason explaining what is missing
   872→      - id: ac-21
   873→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --auto is run
   874→        when: task passes all criteria
   875→        then: task appears with review_for_eligible recommendation but automation field is NOT modified
   876→      - id: ac-22
   877→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --dry-run is run
   878→        when: displaying output
   879→        then: shows what would change without modifying tasks
   880→      - id: ac-23
   881→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --dry-run --auto is run
   882→        when: combining flags
   883→        then: shows auto mode changes without applying them
   884→      - id: ac-24
   885→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --json is run
   886→        when: outputting results
   887→        then: outputs structured JSON with criteria details for each task
   888→      - id: ac-25
   889→        given: kspec tasks assess automation --json is run
   890→        when: outputting results
   891→        then: JSON includes summary counts of recommendations
   892→      - id: ac-26
   893→        given: kspec tasks assess automation is run
   894→        when: no unassessed pending tasks exist
   895→        then: outputs 'No unassessed tasks' message
   896→      - id: ac-27
   897→        given: kspec tasks assess automation is run without --all
   898→        when: filtering tasks
   899→        then: tasks already marked eligible/needs_review/manual_only are skipped
   900→      - id: ac-28
   901→        given: kspec tasks assess automation is run
   902→        when: filtering tasks
   903→        then: non-pending tasks (completed, cancelled, in_progress, blocked) are excluded
   904→    status:
   905→      maturity: draft
   906→      implementation: implemented
   907→requirements:
   908→  - _ulid: 01KFBVD707HVYZZ240A0KMEZ3N
   909→    slugs:
   910→      - task-automation-eligibility
   911→    title: Task Automation Eligibility
   912→    type: requirement
   913→    tags: []
   914→    depends_on: []
   915→    implements: []
   916→    relates_to: []
   917→    tests: []
   918→    notes: []
   919→    created: 2026-01-19T19:23:47.591Z
   920→    description: Tasks have an automation eligibility status that indicates whether they can be
   921→      processed by unattended automation loops (like ralph). Eligibility is determined by human
   922→      judgment during triage - assessing whether the task is unambiguous, appropriately scoped, and
   923→      has sufficient context (spec + notes + description) to be standalone. This prevents automation
   924→      from attempting tasks that require human decisions, clarification, or oversight.
   925→    acceptance_criteria:
   926→      - id: ac-1
   927→        given: a task exists
   928→        when: checking its schema
   929→        then: "it has an optional automation field with enum values: eligible, needs_review, manual_only"
   930→      - id: ac-2
   931→        given: a new task is created
   932→        when: no automation value is specified
   933→        then: the task has no automation field (treated as unassessed)
   934→      - id: ac-3
   935→        given: ralph is selecting tasks
   936→        when: filtering ready tasks
   937→        then: "only tasks with automation: eligible are presented to the agent"
   938→      - id: ac-4
   939→        given: an agent is working on an eligible task
   940→        when: the agent determines the task is not suitable for automation
   941→        then: the agent marks it as needs_review and adds a note explaining why (note is required)
   942→      - id: ac-5
   943→        given: a human is triaging tasks
   944→        when: assessing automation readiness
   945→        then: they can set automation to any value (eligible, needs_review, manual_only) or clear it
   946→      - id: ac-6
   947→        given: a task is marked needs_review
   948→        when: it needs to become eligible again
   949→        then: "a human must review and explicitly set automation: eligible"
   950→      - id: ac-7
   951→        given: ralph is selecting tasks
   952→        when: a task has no automation field (unassessed)
   953→        then: that task is not presented to the agent
   954→      - id: ac-8
   955→        given: ralph is selecting tasks
   956→        when: "a task has automation: needs_review"
   957→        then: that task is not presented to the agent
   958→      - id: ac-9
   959→        given: ralph is selecting tasks
   960→        when: "a task has automation: manual_only"
   961→        then: that task is not presented to the agent
   962→      - id: ac-10
   963→        given: ralph is running
   964→        when: "no tasks with automation: eligible exist in ready state"
   965→        then: ralph exits with a message indicating no eligible tasks available
   966→      - id: ac-11
   967→        given: a user wants to set automation status
   968→        when: running kspec task set @ref --automation eligible
   969→        then: the task's automation field is set to the specified value
   970→      - id: ac-12
   971→        given: a user wants to clear automation status
   972→        when: running kspec task set @ref --no-automation
   973→        then: the task's automation field is removed (returns to unassessed state)
   974→      - id: ac-13
   975→        given: a task is created via kspec task add
   976→        when: the --automation flag is provided
   977→        then: the task is created with the specified automation value
   978→      - id: ac-14
   979→        given: kspec tasks ready is run
   980→        when: displaying the ready tasks list
   981→        then: the automation status is shown for each task (showing 'unassessed' if not set)
   982→      - id: ac-15
   983→        given: a task is marked manual_only
   984→        when: it needs to become eligible
   985→        then: "a human must review and explicitly set automation: eligible"
   986→      - id: ac-16
   987→        given: an agent marks a task as needs_review during a ralph iteration
   988→        when: the marking is complete
   989→        then: the agent moves on to the next eligible task (does not exit the loop)
   990→      - id: ac-17
   991→        given: kspec task get @ref is run
   992→        when: displaying task details
   993→        then: the automation status is shown (or 'unassessed' if not set)
   994→      - id: ac-18
   995→        given: an agent or human marks a task as needs_review
   996→        when: setting the status
   997→        then: a note explaining why the task needs review is required (either via --reason or separate task
   998→          note command)
   999→      - id: ac-19
  1000→        given: kspec tasks ready is run
  1001→        when: the --eligible flag is provided
  1002→        then: "only tasks with automation: eligible are shown"
  1003→      - id: ac-20
  1004→        given: kspec tasks ready is run
  1005→        when: the --unassessed flag is provided
  1006→        then: only tasks without an automation field are shown
  1007→      - id: ac-21
  1008→        given: kspec validate is run
  1009→        when: "a task has automation: eligible but no spec_ref"
  1010→        then: a warning (not error) is emitted suggesting eligible tasks should have linked specs;
  1011→          validation still passes
  1012→      - id: ac-22
  1013→        given: a task's automation status needs to change
  1014→        when: considering valid transitions
  1015→        then: any status can transition to any other status; CLI auto-mode (kspec tasks assess automation
  1016→          --auto) does NOT mark tasks eligible, but agents/humans reviewing interactively CAN mark
  1017→          eligible via kspec task set
  1018→      - id: ac-23
  1019→        given: "a task has automation: eligible"
  1020→        when: its spec_ref is removed or the referenced spec is deleted
  1021→        then: the automation status is preserved but kspec validate emits a warning
  1022→      - id: ac-24
  1023→        given: kspec tasks ready is run
  1024→        when: the --needs-review flag is provided
  1025→        then: "only tasks with automation: needs_review are shown (for human triage)"
  1026→      - id: ac-25
  1027→        given: ralph starts a new loop iteration
  1028→        when: selecting the next task
  1029→        then: "ralph re-reads task list and filters by automation: eligible (reflecting any status changes
  1030→          from previous iterations)"
  1031→    status:
  1032→      maturity: draft
  1033→      implementation: implemented
  1034→  - _ulid: 01KFFFZTA9V1WPHADEDRYJ78XM
  1035→    slugs:
  1036→      - spec-task-reset
  1037→    title: Task Reset Command
  1038→    type: requirement
  1039→    tags: []
  1040→    depends_on: []
  1041→    implements: []
  1042→    relates_to: []
  1043→    tests: []
