  1048→    notes: []
  1049→    created: 2026-01-21T05:21:12.009Z
  1050→    description: New `kspec task reset` command to return any task to pending state, clearing
  1051→      completion-related fields.
  1052→    acceptance_criteria:
  1053→      - id: ac-1
  1054→        given: task has status blocked/cancelled/completed/in_progress/pending_review
  1055→        when: kspec task reset @ref executed
  1056→        then: status becomes pending, timestamps cleared (completed_at, started_at, closed_reason,
  1057→          blocked_by array)
  1058→      - id: ac-2
  1059→        given: task has status pending
  1060→        when: kspec task reset @ref executed
  1061→        then: "error: Task is already pending"
  1062→      - id: ac-3
  1063→        given: task reset succeeds
  1064→        when: operation completes
  1065→        then: shadow commit with message task-reset
  1066→      - id: ac-4
  1067→        given: task reset succeeds
  1068→        when: operation completes
  1069→        then: "note auto-added: Reset from {previous_status} to pending (includes closed_reason if was
  1070→          cancelled)"
  1071→      - id: ac-5
  1072→        given: task A is completed, task B depends on A
  1073→        when: kspec task reset @task-a executed
  1074→        then: A becomes pending; B unaffected (dependency check happens on B's start)
  1075→      - id: ac-6
  1076→        given: JSON mode
  1077→        when: kspec task reset @ref --json executed
  1078→        then: output includes previous_status, new_status, cleared_fields array
  1079→    status:
  1080→      maturity: draft
  1081→      implementation: implemented
  1082→  - _ulid: 01KFFG2WVCZY014JX2CN4S07GS
  1083→    slugs:
  1084→      - spec-completion-enforcement
  1085→    title: Task Completion State Enforcement
  1086→    type: requirement
  1087→    tags: []
  1088→    depends_on: []
  1089→    implements: []
  1090→    relates_to: []
  1091→    tests: []
  1092→    traits:
  1093→      - "@trait-error-guidance"
  1094→      - "@trait-multi-ref-batch"
  1095→    notes: []
  1096→    created: 2026-01-21T05:22:52.908Z
  1097→    description: Enforce that tasks must go through pending_review before completion. The complete
  1098→      command only accepts tasks in pending_review state.
  1099→    acceptance_criteria:
  1100→      - id: ac-1
  1101→        given: task status is pending_review
  1102→        when: kspec task complete @ref executed
  1103→        then: completes successfully
  1104→      - id: ac-2
  1105→        given: task status is in_progress
  1106→        when: kspec task complete @ref executed
  1107→        then: "error: Task must be submitted for review first. Use kspec task submit @ref"
  1108→      - id: ac-3
  1109→        given: task status is pending
  1110→        when: kspec task complete @ref executed
  1111→        then: "error: Task must be started and submitted first"
  1112→      - id: ac-4
  1113→        given: task status is blocked
  1114→        when: kspec task complete @ref executed
  1115→        then: "error: Cannot complete blocked task"
  1116→      - id: ac-5
  1117→        given: task status is cancelled
  1118→        when: kspec task complete @ref executed
  1119→        then: "error: Cannot complete cancelled task. Use kspec task reset @ref first"
  1120→      - id: ac-6
  1121→        given: task status is completed
  1122→        when: kspec task complete @ref executed
  1123→        then: "error: Task is already completed"
  1124→      - id: ac-7
  1125→        given: user wants to skip review
  1126→        when: kspec task complete @ref --skip-review --reason 'Hotfix, no review needed' executed
  1127→        then: bypasses enforcement, completes directly, reason documented in note
  1128→      - id: ac-8
  1129→        given: --skip-review provided without --reason
  1130→        when: kspec task complete @ref --skip-review executed
  1131→        then: "error: --skip-review requires --reason to document why"
  1132→      - id: ac-9
  1133→        given: batch mode with mixed states
  1134→        when: kspec task complete --refs @a @b where @a is pending_review, @b is in_progress
  1135→        then: "@a completes, @b fails with guidance error, exit code 1"
  1136→    status:
  1137→      maturity: draft
  1138→      implementation: implemented
